    "created_at": "2016-08-30T21:58:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-30T21:58:05Z",
    "body": "This is another case for \"some way to opt a DFN out of Bikeshed processing\". I'll go ahead and add that today.\n\n(partials are handled by Bikeshed at the parsing level - if it notices that you're defining a partial interface, it forces the interface name to be an A, rather than choosing A/DFN based on whether there's already an instance of that interface defined elsewhere.  There's nothing at the definition-contract level that indicates something is a partial definition.)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
